        "M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0288"
      ],
      "canonical_claim": "Squirrel Crossing is structured around a moving, flowing trajectory through traffic: the player commits to one continuous vector run, potentially with limited predeclared redirects, exploiting relative motion and vehicle wakes toward a far-side climbable refuge or known vertical anchor. Its strengths are direct speed, leap commitment, and infrastructure use; it does not require convenient vertical anchors in the middle of an ordinary highway. By contrast, Rabbit waits for a broad highway window and Mouse builds continuity from fixed micro-features.",
      "human_question": null,
      "members": [
        {
          "atom_key": "M050-SRC-PA-001::ATOM-PA-DIRECT-0288",
          "disposition": "basis"
